Subject: Backport published SOAP ownership, recursion and response length fixes to PHP 5.6
CVE: CVE-2026-6722, CVE-2026-91765, CVE-2025-14181
Origin: https://github.com/php/php-src/commit/84e3004d25c2ce90f198eb39507489ba73c580aa
Origin: https://github.com/php/php-src/commit/3655b79c7bfa90db004d75a3b282ed0f538f4836
Origin: https://github.com/php/php-src/commit/f7c43b8c72822a4722bd7404c6f65e15b2b912c1
Origin: https://github.com/php/php-src/commit/b11bd1d9390bb203684e3d4aa5e1104ea842de6f
Origin: https://github.com/php/php-src/commit/3aedde06bc329f139de811dc66244ec26c96820c

Based on the published Freexian PHP 7.0 backports. PHP 5.6 stores both XML
serialization nodes and decoded zval pointers in its original reference map.
Keep decoded values in a separate owning map with native addref/destructor APIs;
the serialization map retains its XML node ownership. Keep the published 2048
XML depth and 4096 decoder depth limits. Response bounds use INT_MAX because
PHP 5.6 string lengths and the get_http_body output parameter are int, with
size_t counters and native safe_erealloc. Published tests use PHP 5.6 syntax.
Single-value client responses use refcounted ZVAL_ZVAL transfer because the
new decoding map can retain the temporary zval beyond response unwrapping.

